  message: "P0/P1 SWEEP 2026-08-17, dev 11a240f83d. Every claim below was re-derived against the current tree, not re-read off this thread.\n\nRE-VERIFIED AT TIP, STILL VIOLATED. Production analyze_javascript on a two-file fixture (js + ts), dev 11a240f83d:\n\n    4 call edges emitted, 0 carrying meta.call_construct\n      helper(x)             cc=None\n      fs.readFileSync(x)    cc=None\n      console.log(x)        cc=None\n      console.error(p)      cc=None   (typescript)\n\nContrast the same probe's other languages in the same run: go stamps 3 of 3, python 3 of 4, java 2 of 4. So the zero is a property of the JS/TS analyzer, not of the fixture.\n\nALSO OBSERVED, not previously on this item: obj.write(x) -- an unresolvable instance-method receiver -- emitted NO EDGE AT ALL, so it is not even in the denominator above. That is WI-nasuf's cell, and it means the JS sink surface is losing edges by two mechanisms at once, not one.\n\nThe item's own 'WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED' is unchanged: I did not measure whether JS io-boundary tags actually drop as a result, and did not substitute a proxy for it."  # e868
