  nonce: c770  # c770
  message: "PHASE 0 RE-VERIFICATION AT TIP, 2026-08-25, dev e41a655d6d. REPRODUCES,\nunchanged. js_ts.py contains ZERO occurrences of call_construct at tip\n(grep), and a live fixture confirms it at the edge:\n\n    fs.readFileSync(p)  -> javascript:fs:0-0:readFileSync:unresolved  cc=ABSENT\n    obj.writeThing(p)   -> NO EDGE     (WI-nasuf's emission gap, not this item)\n    plainCall(p)        -> NO EDGE\n    obj.a.b.deep(p)     -> NO EDGE\n\nNote the two defects compound: the edges that DO exist carry no construct, and\nthe instance-method edges that would need one are not emitted at all. Phase 6\n(recall), owner-gated. Status unchanged: violated."  # c770
- op: discuss  # c628
  at: '2026-09-07T11:37:29Z'  # c628
  by: agent  # c628
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c628
  clock: 7  # c628
  nonce: c628  # c628
  message: "RE-VERIFIED AT TIP 2026-09-07 (dev c7e0d943b9) AND THE PREMISE HAS MOVED. Reporting only -- NO status change, no re-prioritisation; the item stays violated for the reason at the end. Instruments: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/gijis_recheck_09072026/ (fx/, probe.py -- the stamp census, gate.py -- the PRODUCTION classify_call path).\n\nTHE FILED CLAIM IS \"ZERO call edges carry meta.call_construct\", last re-verified 2026-08-25 as \"js_ts.py contains ZERO occurrences of call_construct at tip (grep)\". BOTH ARE NOW FALSE. js_ts.py stamps it at three emission sites, and on the item's own fixture shapes 5 of 9 call edges carry it. WI-nasuf (since closed) is what changed it.\n\nWHERE IT IS STAMPED, AND THE PATTERN IS THE RIGHT ONE -- production analyze_javascript, one fixture, js and ts in the same run:\n  fs.readFileSync(p)      module-qualified    slot=fs        cc=ABSENT\n  console.log(x)          named global        slot=console   cc=ABSENT\n  console.error(p)  [ts]  named global        slot=console   cc=ABSENT\n  helper(p)               in-file, RESOLVED   first-party    cc=ABSENT\n  obj.writeThing(p)       untyped receiver    slot=external  cc=method\n  obj.a.b.deep(p)         attribute chain     slot=external  cc=method\n  items.join(',')         untyped receiver    slot=external  cc=method\n  s.normalize()           untyped receiver    slot=external  cc=method\n  obj.readFile(p)         untyped receiver    slot=external  cc=method\nEvery edge that carries NO module slot -- the population the F3 no-module path reads -- now carries `call_construct: method`. The four that lack the field all carry a module slot and never reach that branch. That is the same shape python has had for months and no consumer complains of there.\n\nTHE STATED CONSEQUENCE NO LONGER REPRODUCES, checked BEHAVIOURALLY through the production `classify_call` (not by reading the gate):\n  items.join(',')   -> NONE   (Array.prototype.join vs the catalogued function-kind path.join)\n  s.normalize()     -> NONE   (String.prototype vs path.normalize)\n  obj.readFile(p)   -> NONE   (untyped receiver, a method-kind row's name)\n  fs.readFileSync   -> fs_read/fs.readFileSync   CONTROL, classifies\n  console.log       -> logging/console.log       CONTROL, classifies\nSo the false-positive channel this item describes -- \"F3's method branch is UNCONDITIONAL for JS/TS\", letting a method call on an untyped receiver match a function-kind row by bare name -- is CLOSED at tip. The 2026-08-11 probe found that channel unreachable because no edge existed; it is now reachable AND refused.\n\nA SEPARATE GAP FOUND WHILE CHECKING, filed as its own item: an UNRESOLVED BARE-NAME call emits NO EDGE AT ALL in JS (`join(p)` / `readFileSync(p)` where the name is not defined in the file produced zero edges of any type). That is the JS analogue of the python emission gap INV-mumov filed and #231 closed, and it is why the bare-name half of this item's FP channel is unreachable rather than refused.\n\nWHY THIS ITEM STAYS VIOLATED RATHER THAN SATISFIED. Its own \"WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED\" names the closing evidence and I have NOT produced it: \"a direct io-boundaries run on apollo-server comparing tagged counts against the catalogue's method-kind vs function-kind entries\". A synthetic fixture through the production classifier is strong evidence that the mechanism is fixed; it is not a real-repo count, and this item was filed off real-repo numbers (4,872 edges across 3 repos). The next reader should either run that comparison and close on it, or RE-SCOPE the statement -- \"every analyzer must populate call_construct\" is literally unmet by python too, on edges no consumer reads, so the clause worth keeping is the one about edges that REACH the no-module path."  # c628
