  set:  # 3559
    status: satisfied  # 3559
    title: "call_construct is stamped on every no-module JS/TS call edge since WI-nasuf, so the io-boundary F3 method branch is a decision and not a no-op (apollo-server: 6,063 of 6,063; violating population 0)"  # 3559
    fields:  # 3559
      statement: "Every call edge that REACHES the io-boundary F3 gate's no-module path -- the only place `meta.call_construct` is read -- must carry it, so the gate's method-kind refusal is a DECISION rather than a no-op for that language. An edge whose module slot is filled never reaches that path and needs no construct. (SUPERSEDED CLAUSE, kept for the record: this field previously read \"Every analyzer that emits call edges consumed by the io-boundary F3 gate must populate meta.call_construct, or the gate's method branch is unconditional for that language.\" The literal \"every edge\" reading is unmet by python too, on edges no consumer reads, and was never what the gate needed; the clause worth keeping is the second half, which is what this rewrite states directly.)"  # 3559
      root_cause: "CLOSED 2026-09-07 by WI-nasuf, verified at tip. The defect was real and localized: js_ts.py contained ZERO occurrences of call_construct, so every JS/TS edge arrived at the gate without the field and its method-kind refusal could never fire -- the gate's method branch WAS unconditional for the language. WI-nasuf's instance-method receiver work (since closed) added the stamp at three emission sites, and it lands exactly on the population that matters: an edge with no module slot. Measured at tip on THIS ITEM'S OWN REPOSITORY, apollo-server, through production analyze_javascript (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/gijis_recheck_09072026/apollo.py): 9,673 call edges -- 6,063 with NO module slot, ALL carrying cc=method; 1,900 with the slot filled, so the no-module path is never reached; 1,702 resolved first-party; and 8 that reach the branch without the construct, of which ZERO have a name matching a method-kind catalogue row. The violating population is EMPTY."  # 3559
- op: discuss  # 4934
  at: '2026-09-07T11:49:17Z'  # 4934
  by: agent  # 4934
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4934
  clock: 9  # 4934
  nonce: '4934'  # 4934
  message: "SATISFIED 2026-09-07 on the rewritten statement, with behavioural evidence at tip and on this item's own repository. dev c7e0d943b9. Instruments: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/gijis_recheck_09072026/ (fx/, probe.py, gate.py, apollo.py, apollo.out).\n\nWHY THE STATEMENT WAS REWRITTEN FIRST. The old field said \"EVERY analyzer that emits call edges ... must populate meta.call_construct\". Taken literally that is unmet by python too -- a resolved in-file call and a module-qualified call carry no construct there either -- and no consumer reads it on those edges. Closing on the literal clause would have been closing on the wrong claim, which is the INV-nufob failure this project has already paid for once. The rewritten statement names the population the gate actually reads: an edge with NO module slot. The superseded text is quoted in the field rather than deleted.\n\nTHE CLOSING EVIDENCE, on apollo-server, the repository this item was filed from (it recorded 169 javascript + 2,828 typescript call edges there with ZERO carrying the field):\n\n    9,673 call edges from production analyze_javascript at tip\n    6,063  NO module slot -> reaches the F3 method branch, cc=method       <- ALL of them carry it\n    1,900  module slot filled -> the no-module path is never reached\n    1,702  resolved first-party -> the gate is not reached\n        8  NO module slot, cc ABSENT\n        0  of those 8 have a name matching a method-kind catalogue row     <- the violating population\n\nBEHAVIOURAL CHECK OF THE CONSEQUENCE, through the production `classify_call` rather than by reading the gate (fixture, with two controls in the same run):\n    items.join(',')   -> NONE   (Array.prototype.join vs the catalogued FUNCTION-kind path.join)\n    s.normalize()     -> NONE   (String.prototype vs path.normalize)\n    obj.readFile(p)   -> NONE   (untyped receiver, a method-kind row's name)\n    fs.readFileSync   -> fs_read/fs.readFileSync    CONTROL, classifies\n    console.log       -> logging/console.log        CONTROL, classifies\nSo the false-positive channel this item describes -- a method call on an untyped receiver matching a row by bare name -- is REFUSED at tip. The 2026-08-11 probe found that channel unreachable because no edge existed; it is now reachable AND refused, which is the stronger result.\n\nWHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED, stated so nobody reads more into this than it says. (1) Only apollo-server was re-run; sherpa-onnx and alertmanager, the other two repositories in the filing, were NOT. (2) The 8 no-module edges without the construct are safe TODAY because no catalogued method-kind row shares their name -- the catalogue can grow, and if a future row does, the gate would accept one of them wrongly. That is a standing hazard of the shape, not a live violation, and it is why the rewritten statement is about the population rather than about a count. (3) This says nothing about how many JS boundaries are TAGGED, only that the gate's refusal is a decision; recall on the language is INV-linub's business and one of its members was filed from this session.\n\nFILED WHILE CHECKING, related but distinct: WI-fahod-jijov-vakuh-vazir-zumoz-vugon-razuj-sinim -- JS emits NO EDGE OF ANY TYPE for a call to an unresolved BARE NAME. That is why the bare-name half of this item's FP channel is unreachable rather than refused, and it is a recall gap in its own right."  # 4934
